From ac5ce7bc06954fcd09429e8a47c3e4da846edec5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Seyoon Ragavan <complexzetaprime@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:57:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Build/InputRewind: the input rewind as a machine, and two
 relabelings as one

A new module with the native input head's rewind (one step left, the scan
left over the input, one step right into a stationary park): its run from a
start configuration with the head at p >= 1 reaches the park at exactly time
p + 1 and not earlier, with the head at 1, and leaves the work tapes, the
work heads and the output unchanged at every time. Also
Cfg.mapState_mapState, the composite of two state relabelings.

Build/NDHost's private guessRun_mapState_mapState had the new lemma's
statement; it is removed and its three uses rewrite with the public lemma.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

